1
00:00:38,205 --> 00:00:40,707
- Oh, no.
- Wait...

2
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:44,002
- Ms. Gong?
- Mr. Dokgo.

3
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:47,673
Why are you doing this to me?

4
00:00:48,757 --> 00:00:50,175
What do you mean?

5
00:00:50,509 --> 00:00:51,760
You started it this time.

6
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:53,387
Mr. Dokgo.

7
00:00:54,429 --> 00:00:56,181
But you're gay.

8
00:00:57,391 --> 00:00:58,392
I'm sorry?

9
00:01:00,227 --> 00:01:01,228
I'm what?

10
00:01:01,562 --> 00:01:04,481
You're into guys.

11
00:01:04,815 --> 00:01:05,816
Who said that?

12
00:01:06,608 --> 00:01:10,279
I saw the way you were with Mr. Yun.

13
00:01:10,904 --> 00:01:11,905
"Mr. Yun"?

14
00:01:11,989 --> 00:01:12,990
You mean Ji-o?

15
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:16,451
That's not true.

16
00:01:16,535 --> 00:01:19,663
You really don't have
to hide it from me.

17
00:01:19,997 --> 00:01:21,248
In fact, I...

18
00:01:21,665 --> 00:01:24,251
I've witnessed it
several times already.

19
00:01:24,334 --> 00:01:27,045
No, you're wrong.
He's just a very good friend.

20
00:01:30,257 --> 00:01:31,508
I like women.

21
00:01:37,598 --> 00:01:39,558
- Really?
- Do you want me to prove it?

22
00:01:40,934 --> 00:01:42,894
- What?
- Then let's go to my place.

23
00:01:43,562 --> 00:01:44,688
I'm totally down.

24
00:01:46,607 --> 00:01:49,151
I don't understand.

25
00:01:49,234 --> 00:01:51,236
I can show you that I'm straight.

26
00:01:55,365 --> 00:01:57,784
You're joking.

27
00:02:02,331 --> 00:02:03,624
I'm not joking.

28
00:02:10,881 --> 00:02:12,716
What just happened

29
00:02:13,550 --> 00:02:14,760
did not happen.

30
00:02:18,555 --> 00:02:21,350
I'm sorry for the misunderstanding.

31
00:02:44,498 --> 00:02:47,125
Am I feeling relieved right now?

32
00:02:51,088 --> 00:02:52,798
You're crazy, Yeon-su.

33
00:02:58,762 --> 00:03:01,306
Let's separate.

34
00:03:01,390 --> 00:03:04,476
Don't say that, sweetheart.
I just made ratatouille.

35
00:03:05,727 --> 00:03:07,604
The tomato sauce is simply the best.

36
00:03:08,355 --> 00:03:10,482
- Where did that come from?
- I'm sick of this.

37
00:03:10,899 --> 00:03:13,193
I'm over 30,
and people still think I'm gay.

38
00:03:13,276 --> 00:03:14,361
It happens all the time.

39
00:03:14,444 --> 00:03:17,280
You might as well
just accept your fate.

40
00:03:17,364 --> 00:03:19,241
But why? Who thinks you're gay?

41
00:03:20,450 --> 00:03:21,451
Gong Yeon-su.

42
00:03:24,538 --> 00:03:26,248
- Let's separate.
- You just said it was fate.

43
00:03:26,331 --> 00:03:28,125
It's time we fought against it.

44
00:03:28,417 --> 00:03:29,543
We're over 30 now.

45
00:03:29,626 --> 00:03:31,294
Cheers to our separation.

46
00:03:42,264 --> 00:03:46,727
MAKE ME TINGLE

47
00:03:48,395 --> 00:03:50,313
EPISODE 4

48
00:03:51,148 --> 00:03:53,150
For a passionate night
with my girlfriend?

49
00:03:54,276 --> 00:03:55,485
We barely do it.

50
00:03:57,195 --> 00:03:59,614
I don't know.
He says he's always tired.

51
00:04:01,324 --> 00:04:04,995
I want it to be a special night.

52
00:04:05,537 --> 00:04:07,789
Actually, it'd be
my first experience.

53
00:04:07,873 --> 00:04:09,624
Your first time?
That's pretty important.

54
00:04:09,708 --> 00:04:13,086
Sex gets boring when you do
the same thing every time.

55
00:04:14,296 --> 00:04:15,630
I think it'd be fun.

56
00:04:15,714 --> 00:04:17,507
My boyfriend would love it too.

57
00:04:18,592 --> 00:04:19,634
The fun is a big part of it.

58
00:04:19,718 --> 00:04:22,345
So what should be included
in the random box?

59
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:24,055
My honest opinion?

60
00:04:24,139 --> 00:04:26,224
Well, let me think.

61
00:04:26,767 --> 00:04:28,935
- Something romantic.
- Romantic?

62
00:04:29,019 --> 00:04:31,146
Something unexpected.
It'd be disappointing

63
00:04:31,229 --> 00:04:32,397
to find the same old things.

64
00:04:32,856 --> 00:04:33,857
My thoughts, exactly.

65
00:04:35,066 --> 00:04:36,151
Let's open them.

66
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:42,783
Only sex toys inside?

67
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:45,160
A perfume and a candle?

68
00:04:46,203 --> 00:04:47,370
Our random box

69
00:04:48,121 --> 00:04:49,706
isn't a toy for kids.

70
00:04:50,290 --> 00:04:52,459
You said the fun was a part of it.

71
00:04:52,542 --> 00:04:53,835
Also, it's supposed to be eventful.

72
00:04:54,085 --> 00:04:56,421
These are too hardcore.

73
00:04:56,505 --> 00:04:57,672
Still, this won't work.

74
00:04:58,340 --> 00:04:59,758
This is 200mL.

75
00:05:00,091 --> 00:05:02,010
That means this won't work either.

76
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:03,762
This is 250mL.

77
00:05:04,596 --> 00:05:06,056
It's necessary.

78
00:05:08,016 --> 00:05:11,436
Are you giving up on the surprise,
fun, and romance?

79
00:05:11,520 --> 00:05:12,979
Efficiency is what matters most.

80
00:05:13,438 --> 00:05:15,357
It won't be fun
if there's not much to it.

81
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:18,360
But I think you're focusing
a little too much on efficiency.

82
00:05:20,487 --> 00:05:22,405
Why do you think I added this?

83
00:05:22,781 --> 00:05:26,576
This lube helps reduce friction
and ease the pain.

84
00:05:27,077 --> 00:05:30,330
For some people, it may be essential
depending on their condition.

85
00:05:31,039 --> 00:05:32,999
The demand is surprisingly high

86
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:34,376
and the cost is fairly low.

87
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:37,754
It offers much more value
in terms of need and efficiency

88
00:05:38,380 --> 00:05:40,799
than something like scented candles.

89
00:05:41,132 --> 00:05:44,010
Plus, the perfume and the candle
aren't even our products.

90
00:05:44,719 --> 00:05:47,722
Obviously, we need to take
the cost into consideration.

91
00:06:04,531 --> 00:06:07,075
I get his point about the perfume.

92
00:06:07,158 --> 00:06:09,411
But wasn't the candle
a pretty good idea?

93
00:06:09,494 --> 00:06:11,288
Doesn't he get romance?

94
00:06:13,498 --> 00:06:16,543
Well, what would I expect from a guy
who thinks love is

95
00:06:16,626 --> 00:06:18,336
just a reproductive urge?

96
00:06:19,170 --> 00:06:23,133
If all we care about is efficiency,
why are we even making random boxes?

97
00:06:23,216 --> 00:06:25,010
We could just sell them as a bundle.

98
00:06:25,093 --> 00:06:26,177
Hey, Ms. Gong.

99
00:06:26,678 --> 00:06:29,055
Is that man
the only thing on your mind?

100
00:06:29,848 --> 00:06:33,935
Gosh, you've been rattling on
about him for days.

101
00:06:34,019 --> 00:06:37,314
You're seriously obsessed.

102
00:06:37,397 --> 00:06:39,524
What are you talking about?
I'm not obsessed.

103
00:06:39,608 --> 00:06:40,901
What? Hey.

104
00:06:44,279 --> 00:06:46,281
Yeon-su, give it to me straight.

105
00:06:46,823 --> 00:06:48,491
Are you glad he's not gay?

106
00:06:48,575 --> 00:06:49,618
Not at all.

107
00:06:49,701 --> 00:06:52,871
It's none of my business
whether he's gay or not.

108
00:06:52,954 --> 00:06:55,665
Then why the test kiss?

109
00:06:55,749 --> 00:06:57,667
What were you trying to figure out?

110
00:06:59,794 --> 00:07:00,837
Tell me.

111
00:07:01,463 --> 00:07:02,714
Say something.

112
00:07:05,508 --> 00:07:06,927
Try some of this.

113
00:07:11,598 --> 00:07:13,558
- Baek-hee.
- Yes?

114
00:07:13,934 --> 00:07:15,769
So when's a good time?

115
00:07:16,519 --> 00:07:18,188
Any time works for me.

116
00:07:19,689 --> 00:07:22,233
What do old folks like us
have to be busy with?

117
00:07:22,317 --> 00:07:23,401
Exactly.

118
00:07:23,485 --> 00:07:25,487
It's you young people who are busy.

119
00:07:26,154 --> 00:07:27,155
Yeon-su.

120
00:07:27,572 --> 00:07:29,908
- When's a good time for you?
- Me?

121
00:07:30,617 --> 00:07:33,745
Well, I'm not sure.
I have to check my schedule.

122
00:07:34,204 --> 00:07:35,413
Would he like chicken?

123
00:07:36,289 --> 00:07:38,792
Most people like chicken.

124
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:41,002
But what is this for?
Are we having guests?

125
00:07:41,461 --> 00:07:42,921
We're inviting Mr. Dokgo for a meal.

126
00:07:46,967 --> 00:07:48,593
Inviting who?

127
00:07:48,677 --> 00:07:51,304
He came all this way before,
and we just let him leave.

128
00:07:51,388 --> 00:07:53,139
That's no way to treat a guest.

129
00:07:53,473 --> 00:07:54,849
Of course not.

130
00:07:56,726 --> 00:07:58,687
I'll treat him to a meal separately.

131
00:07:58,770 --> 00:08:00,355
It's just a meal.

132
00:08:00,647 --> 00:08:02,273
We'll keep it simple
and make <i>samgyetang.</i>

133
00:08:02,357 --> 00:08:03,733
Just ask if he likes chicken.

134
00:08:05,318 --> 00:08:07,612
I'll treat him to a proper meal
at a famous place

135
00:08:08,196 --> 00:08:09,489
that specializes in native chicken.

136
00:08:11,533 --> 00:08:13,368
When an elder tells you something...

137
00:08:14,786 --> 00:08:15,996
Don't argue. Just bring him.

138
00:08:24,379 --> 00:08:26,047
Okay, Grandpa.

139
00:08:29,551 --> 00:08:30,552
Invite him.

140
00:08:31,428 --> 00:08:33,013
ELECTRICAL INSPECTION
POWER OUTAGE NOTICE

141
00:08:33,096 --> 00:08:35,724
<i>This is an announcement</i>
<i>from the management office.</i>

142
00:08:35,807 --> 00:08:37,767
<i>Due to an electrical inspection</i>

143
00:08:37,851 --> 00:08:41,855
<i>the power will be out</i>
<i>from 7 to 7:30 p.m...</i>

144
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:08,882
<i>I've been thinking.</i>

145
00:09:10,925 --> 00:09:13,303
The candle should be included
in the random box.

146
00:09:14,387 --> 00:09:15,930
I thought we were done
talking about this.

147
00:09:16,014 --> 00:09:18,850
Ms. Gong still can't let go
of the candle.

148
00:09:19,392 --> 00:09:21,186
It's starting again.

149
00:09:21,269 --> 00:09:24,147
Without this,
the random box loses its purpose.

150
00:09:24,522 --> 00:09:27,067
I don't mind dropping the perfume,
Jenga, or bath bombs

151
00:09:27,150 --> 00:09:31,071
but this candle has to stay.

152
00:09:31,154 --> 00:09:32,155
Convince me.

153
00:09:32,238 --> 00:09:35,200
Why are you so determined to keep it?

154
00:09:37,452 --> 00:09:39,204
You really don't get it, do you?

155
00:09:39,871 --> 00:09:43,792
There's one crucial thing
missing from this box.

156
00:09:43,875 --> 00:09:45,710
- Which is?
- Emotion.

157
00:09:46,002 --> 00:09:48,421
Something for the heart,
not just the body.

158
00:09:48,505 --> 00:09:52,050
That cozy warmth and romantic mood
you only get from candlelight, no?

159
00:09:56,679 --> 00:09:57,680
It's unnecessary.

160
00:10:00,809 --> 00:10:02,102
That was a hard no.

161
00:10:02,352 --> 00:10:04,938
How disappointing.

162
00:10:06,689 --> 00:10:08,316
Is she going in?

163
00:10:08,399 --> 00:10:09,984
- She is.
- She's going.

164
00:10:15,406 --> 00:10:19,202
- Are you doing this on purpose?
- Doing what?

165
00:10:20,745 --> 00:10:23,581
Do you not understand what I'm saying

166
00:10:23,665 --> 00:10:25,416
or are you choosing not to?

167
00:10:27,836 --> 00:10:29,337
I simply don't understand.

168
00:10:29,587 --> 00:10:31,297
Do you know why you don't?

169
00:10:32,090 --> 00:10:35,593
You're only focused on selling
the mystery concept.

170
00:10:35,969 --> 00:10:37,887
You just want to fill the box

171
00:10:37,971 --> 00:10:40,390
with practical, high-performing
products that have enough demand

172
00:10:40,473 --> 00:10:43,101
fit the price point,
and make good business sense.

173
00:10:43,184 --> 00:10:44,352
Any problem with that?

174
00:10:44,811 --> 00:10:46,980
It sounds perfectly sensible to me.

175
00:10:47,063 --> 00:10:49,357
Why people look forward
to the surprise

176
00:10:49,607 --> 00:10:51,484
what makes them smile

177
00:10:51,776 --> 00:10:54,487
or how it helps couples
connect emotionally.

178
00:10:54,571 --> 00:10:55,947
You never consider these.

179
00:10:56,656 --> 00:11:00,827
To me, that candle is
what defines this random box.

180
00:11:00,910 --> 00:11:05,582
It shows that this company cares
about the heart, not just the body.

181
00:11:06,166 --> 00:11:08,334
Just like you analyze
what satisfies people

182
00:11:08,418 --> 00:11:11,171
I analyze their emotions
and consumer desires.

183
00:11:11,254 --> 00:11:13,339
At least in this field

184
00:11:13,423 --> 00:11:16,259
I know a little more
than you do, Mr. Dokgo.

185
00:11:16,342 --> 00:11:19,012
Didn't my ad resonate with you enough
to come find me?

186
00:11:19,095 --> 00:11:20,513
Then you should trust me.

187
00:11:29,355 --> 00:11:30,690
- What?
- What?

188
00:11:30,773 --> 00:11:33,193
Why aren't you saying anything?

189
00:11:33,276 --> 00:11:35,695
You're not entirely wrong.

190
00:11:36,529 --> 00:11:39,073
Are we adding the candle then?

191
00:11:39,157 --> 00:11:42,285
You have a fair point,
but I'm not completely convinced.

192
00:12:07,143 --> 00:12:08,478
I'm with you on the candle.

193
00:12:13,816 --> 00:12:19,072
Still, the company has to think
about the cost of the candles

194
00:12:19,656 --> 00:12:23,034
and Dal is responsible for keeping
the risk as low as possible.

195
00:12:25,036 --> 00:12:28,623
This campaign shouldn't be
about playing it safe.

196
00:12:29,082 --> 00:12:34,295
It should be about shaping
how consumers see this company.

197
00:12:35,546 --> 00:12:38,466
Isn't that why you put me
in charge of brand marketing?

198
00:12:38,841 --> 00:12:41,552
You're right, Ms. Gong.

199
00:12:41,636 --> 00:12:44,138
Brand marketing is
about shaping the image first.

200
00:12:45,807 --> 00:12:49,185
I'll talk to the candle company
this week

201
00:12:49,269 --> 00:12:51,479
and see what kind of price
we can work out.

202
00:12:53,773 --> 00:12:54,774
You never give up.

203
00:12:56,442 --> 00:12:57,777
We should still get off work.

204
00:12:58,027 --> 00:13:00,738
Want to grab dinner?
How about some spicy udon?

205
00:13:01,864 --> 00:13:04,200
No, thank you.
I still have some work left.

206
00:13:04,534 --> 00:13:06,452
Come on, just a quick bowl of udon.

207
00:13:07,328 --> 00:13:09,706
I have to get home
and feed my fish too.

208
00:13:14,585 --> 00:13:15,628
Something spicy.

209
00:13:27,181 --> 00:13:30,059
Do you know
the udon place we're going to?

210
00:13:30,143 --> 00:13:32,437
No, I don't. Is it far from here?

211
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:34,022
We've been there before.

212
00:13:34,105 --> 00:13:36,065
- Really?
- For a team dinner.

213
00:13:37,066 --> 00:13:38,443
They have really nice food.

214
00:13:48,703 --> 00:13:49,704
HAE, BYEOL'S MOM

215
00:13:49,787 --> 00:13:51,122
<i>Please come this time.</i>

216
00:13:51,205 --> 00:13:53,291
<i>Hae and Byeol really miss you.</i>

217
00:13:53,374 --> 00:13:54,584
<i>I'd appreciate it.</i>

218
00:14:08,389 --> 00:14:11,100
- Set it up here.
- Yes, sir.

219
00:14:22,195 --> 00:14:23,279
Thank you.

220
00:14:26,324 --> 00:14:27,325
Thank you.

221
00:14:34,123 --> 00:14:35,208
You don't like crown daisy?

222
00:14:36,417 --> 00:14:39,462
Not really.
I'm not a fan of the grassy taste.

223
00:14:46,135 --> 00:14:48,262
Mr. Yun, you seem like the type

224
00:14:48,763 --> 00:14:51,182
who eats whatever his girlfriend
leaves behind

225
00:14:51,265 --> 00:14:52,975
when she's full or picky about food.

226
00:14:53,476 --> 00:14:54,477
Isn't that normal?

227
00:14:55,061 --> 00:14:57,480
No, not everyone does that.

228
00:14:58,523 --> 00:15:00,483
I see it as a privilege.

229
00:15:01,734 --> 00:15:03,778
That's something you can only do
for someone you like.

230
00:15:05,822 --> 00:15:07,448
Yeah, I think you're right.

231
00:15:08,783 --> 00:15:11,202
Which one do you like more?
Steamed bun or fish-shaped pastry?

232
00:15:11,285 --> 00:15:12,453
- Now?
- Yes.

233
00:15:13,496 --> 00:15:14,539
Fish-shaped pastry.

234
00:15:14,622 --> 00:15:16,290
- <i>Ramyeon </i>or udon?
- Udon.

235
00:15:17,166 --> 00:15:18,668
Got it. I'll remember that.

236
00:15:19,836 --> 00:15:21,587
- Dig in.
- Bon appétit.

237
00:15:21,671 --> 00:15:22,755
Bon appétit.

238
00:15:30,596 --> 00:15:31,597
It's delicious.

239
00:15:34,976 --> 00:15:36,853
<i>Security mode turned off.</i>

240
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:49,949
Everyone from Loand has also left.

241
00:15:50,032 --> 00:15:51,868
No one's inside the building.

242
00:15:51,951 --> 00:15:52,994
<i>Roger that.</i>

243
00:15:53,077 --> 00:15:54,620
<i>Power will go out in five minutes.</i>

244
00:16:05,506 --> 00:16:08,384
<i>It's normal to have</i>
<i>disagreements at work.</i>

245
00:16:08,926 --> 00:16:11,429
And honestly,
Dal can be a little difficult.

246
00:16:14,265 --> 00:16:15,725
I won't argue with that.

247
00:16:17,059 --> 00:16:18,561
Give him a little time.

248
00:16:19,103 --> 00:16:22,732
Dal isn't very good
at opening up to people.

249
00:16:23,191 --> 00:16:26,194
He once said to me over drinks

250
00:16:26,819 --> 00:16:29,864
that there's no door handle
to his heart.

251
00:16:30,198 --> 00:16:32,783
What does he mean by that?

252
00:16:33,951 --> 00:16:35,203
I guess he means it literally.

253
00:16:35,453 --> 00:16:37,914
What happens when a door is shut
and there's no handle?

254
00:16:38,915 --> 00:16:42,251
No one can get in.

255
00:16:43,252 --> 00:16:44,587
But the problem is

256
00:16:45,421 --> 00:16:47,882
he can't get out either.

257
00:16:48,633 --> 00:16:52,929
That's when I started acting
like a puppy around him.

258
00:16:53,638 --> 00:16:56,516
I have to keep making noise
at the door

259
00:16:56,599 --> 00:16:59,060
just to get a response
through the crack in the door.

260
00:17:16,619 --> 00:17:17,620
What the heck?

261
00:18:16,762 --> 00:18:18,097
A ghost!

262
00:18:18,889 --> 00:18:19,890
Get away!

263
00:18:20,850 --> 00:18:23,644
Mr. Dokgo?

264
00:18:32,486 --> 00:18:34,864
Oh, Ms. Gong?

265
00:18:35,573 --> 00:18:37,867
Are you okay?

266
00:18:47,752 --> 00:18:48,753
Yes.

267
00:19:06,062 --> 00:19:07,688
I thought you left.

268
00:19:07,772 --> 00:19:11,192
I had a few things to finish.

269
00:19:11,525 --> 00:19:13,110
I came back after dinner

270
00:19:13,486 --> 00:19:15,446
and I heard
about the electrical inspection.

271
00:19:15,529 --> 00:19:17,114
So I came up to grab my bag.

272
00:19:18,324 --> 00:19:21,202
They should've given us a heads-up
about the inspection.

273
00:19:21,452 --> 00:19:22,495
They did.

274
00:19:22,953 --> 00:19:23,996
Really?

275
00:19:24,080 --> 00:19:27,667
They put up the notice in the lobby
and in the elevator.

276
00:19:27,750 --> 00:19:28,959
They even made announcements.

277
00:19:29,502 --> 00:19:30,503
Did they?

278
00:19:33,422 --> 00:19:35,758
Are you afraid of the dark?

279
00:19:36,926 --> 00:19:40,054
- Who said that?
- Are you afraid of ghosts?

280
00:19:48,979 --> 00:19:52,525
Actually, I used to be afraid
of the rain.

281
00:19:52,817 --> 00:19:54,735
I told you
I didn't like the rain, right?

282
00:19:56,362 --> 00:19:58,322
You don't have to comfort me.

283
00:19:59,240 --> 00:20:00,908
It only makes me uncomfortable.

284
00:20:00,991 --> 00:20:04,829
I'm not trying to comfort you.

285
00:20:05,121 --> 00:20:06,706
It's because of the candle.

286
00:20:06,789 --> 00:20:09,875
Funny how looking at this
gets me talking.

287
00:20:18,759 --> 00:20:23,806
When I was little,
I once got locked in the bathroom.

288
00:20:23,889 --> 00:20:26,934
No matter how much I screamed,
my parents didn't come

289
00:20:27,601 --> 00:20:29,437
because of the sound of the rain.

290
00:20:31,689 --> 00:20:34,400
It felt like the rain
was swallowing my voice

291
00:20:35,234 --> 00:20:36,694
and that terrified me.

292
00:20:54,628 --> 00:20:58,632
I still don't like it,
but I'm not afraid of it anymore.

293
00:20:59,383 --> 00:21:02,845
I realized what I felt back then
wasn't really fear.

294
00:21:02,928 --> 00:21:05,014
It was sadness.

295
00:21:06,056 --> 00:21:08,851
Once I understood
what that feeling actually was

296
00:21:08,934 --> 00:21:10,352
I felt better.

297
00:21:13,939 --> 00:21:16,150
What would it be for you, Mr. Dokgo?

298
00:21:16,984 --> 00:21:20,321
What could've been
the feeling underneath the fear?

299
00:21:26,660 --> 00:21:28,662
Dad!

300
00:21:29,288 --> 00:21:31,165
Mom!

301
00:21:31,457 --> 00:21:35,503
Dad!

302
00:21:38,297 --> 00:21:39,298
<i>Probably...</i>

303
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:42,301
<i>loneliness.</i>

304
00:22:12,748 --> 00:22:15,000
Wasn't it quite useful?

305
00:22:16,627 --> 00:22:17,670
So are you saying

306
00:22:18,379 --> 00:22:21,674
this candle made us have
that cringey conversation?

307
00:22:21,757 --> 00:22:24,718
Just enough darkness,
just enough light

308
00:22:25,719 --> 00:22:29,014
a little warmth, and the right mood.

309
00:22:29,431 --> 00:22:31,600
Every romance needs them.

310
00:22:33,477 --> 00:22:34,478
Was that

311
00:22:36,105 --> 00:22:37,648
romance just now?

312
00:22:40,484 --> 00:22:41,485
Sorry?

313
00:22:44,947 --> 00:22:47,032
No, I mean, what do you...

314
00:22:48,701 --> 00:22:50,661
I was referring
to the random box, not us.

315
00:22:51,871 --> 00:22:55,249
Let's give random box buyers
a touch of romance.

316
00:22:55,332 --> 00:22:57,084
Something like that.

317
00:23:00,880 --> 00:23:02,590
Well, the lights are back on

318
00:23:03,132 --> 00:23:05,134
so I'll be heading out.

319
00:23:06,218 --> 00:23:09,013
By the way, Mr. Dokgo...

320
00:23:09,972 --> 00:23:12,433
- I'm sure you hate <i>samgyetang, </i>no?
- No.

321
00:23:13,183 --> 00:23:14,518
I don't hate it.

322
00:23:14,602 --> 00:23:17,479
- Any chicken allergies?
- None.

323
00:23:18,522 --> 00:23:19,648
- Why?
- What?

324
00:23:22,651 --> 00:23:24,528
Never mind.

325
00:23:24,612 --> 00:23:25,988
I'll be going, then.

326
00:24:05,319 --> 00:24:07,154
THANK YOU, MOM AND DAD

327
00:24:09,198 --> 00:24:11,116
DAD, MOM, HAE, ME

328
00:24:19,583 --> 00:24:20,918
- You came.
- Yes.

329
00:24:22,711 --> 00:24:24,964
Girls, look who's here.

330
00:24:29,885 --> 00:24:31,345
Dal!

331
00:24:31,428 --> 00:24:32,429
Dal!

332
00:24:32,846 --> 00:24:35,516
- Come here, Hae and Byeol.
- Dal!

333
00:24:35,849 --> 00:24:38,143
- There.
- You finally came.

334
00:24:38,227 --> 00:24:41,438
We want to play with you,
but you never come.

335
00:24:42,064 --> 00:24:44,984
I'm sorry. I'm busy all the time.

336
00:24:45,067 --> 00:24:46,068
Wait here.

337
00:24:48,862 --> 00:24:51,156
- They're for you.
- Wow, it's so pretty.

338
00:24:51,865 --> 00:24:54,243
Let's open it over there.

339
00:24:55,494 --> 00:24:57,329
- He's over there.
- It's so pretty!

340
00:25:06,046 --> 00:25:07,214
Happy birthday.

341
00:25:07,673 --> 00:25:09,925
Let's skip the small talk.

342
00:25:10,592 --> 00:25:12,177
You've had enough fun.

343
00:25:12,720 --> 00:25:14,346
Come back to the company now.

344
00:25:14,430 --> 00:25:16,807
You've dragged my name
through the mud enough.

345
00:25:17,850 --> 00:25:18,892
I'm not done having fun yet.

346
00:25:18,976 --> 00:25:20,352
You insolent brat.

347
00:25:20,894 --> 00:25:22,521
You can't get investors

348
00:25:22,604 --> 00:25:24,064
and you can't even
market it properly.

349
00:25:24,314 --> 00:25:25,774
And you still call that a business?

350
00:25:25,858 --> 00:25:27,609
You seem invested in my company.

351
00:25:27,693 --> 00:25:29,903
It's stupid to cling to something
that's not working.

352
00:25:30,279 --> 00:25:33,407
If you're a man, you should have
the guts to walk away!

353
00:25:33,490 --> 00:25:35,325
- Like you did with your marriage?
- What?

354
00:25:35,409 --> 00:25:38,787
I may lack your decisiveness,
but endurance is one thing I've got.

355
00:25:39,038 --> 00:25:40,622
I'll play this out for now.

356
00:25:40,873 --> 00:25:42,666
Let's talk again
around your 60th birthday.

357
00:25:43,042 --> 00:25:45,711
Who on earth did you get
that stubborn streak from?

358
00:25:45,794 --> 00:25:48,338
I hate to admit it,
but the stubbornness, the arrogance

359
00:25:48,422 --> 00:25:49,631
and even the womanizing...

360
00:25:50,215 --> 00:25:51,258
I got it all from you.

361
00:25:53,177 --> 00:25:54,386
I'll be off now.

362
00:26:07,357 --> 00:26:09,526
Oh, seriously?

363
00:26:09,860 --> 00:26:11,320
We should air this place out.

364
00:26:12,488 --> 00:26:16,075
Do you know how funny you looked
eating that cake?

365
00:26:18,577 --> 00:26:19,828
Today was so much fun.

366
00:26:19,912 --> 00:26:22,414
Our shots were really on point...

367
00:26:25,250 --> 00:26:26,585
- Are you okay?
- Yeah.

368
00:26:52,152 --> 00:26:53,695
- Yes?
<i>- So?</i>

369
00:26:54,154 --> 00:26:55,864
<i>When are you visiting</i>
<i>her family again?</i>

370
00:26:56,240 --> 00:26:59,284
<i>I heard they took</i>
<i>quite a liking to you.</i>

371
00:27:04,998 --> 00:27:06,917
I'm home.

372
00:27:09,169 --> 00:27:10,170
Wait.

373
00:27:11,296 --> 00:27:13,006
Did you ask him when he's available?

374
00:27:13,465 --> 00:27:14,550
For what?

375
00:27:14,633 --> 00:27:15,884
I'm talking about Mr. Dokgo.

376
00:27:15,968 --> 00:27:17,928
Mom, why would you...

377
00:27:18,011 --> 00:27:19,805
I said I'll treat him myself.

378
00:27:19,888 --> 00:27:20,889
Just invite him.

379
00:27:21,390 --> 00:27:23,142
Not happening.

380
00:27:23,684 --> 00:27:25,561
Do you know who your grandma called?

381
00:27:25,978 --> 00:27:26,979
Your ninth-degree relative.

382
00:27:27,604 --> 00:27:29,356
What about my ninth-degree relative?

383
00:27:29,439 --> 00:27:30,482
Don't you remember?

384
00:27:30,816 --> 00:27:32,484
He set you up with Mr. Dokgo.

385
00:27:34,486 --> 00:27:36,613
- What do I do?
- You know what to do.

386
00:27:56,008 --> 00:27:58,135
The candle's officially in!

387
00:27:59,803 --> 00:28:02,514
- Is this our final version?
- Yes.

388
00:28:04,266 --> 00:28:05,267
USER GUIDE

389
00:28:05,559 --> 00:28:07,561
Min-hyung, are you good with coding?

390
00:28:07,644 --> 00:28:09,396
You bet I am. Why?

391
00:28:09,897 --> 00:28:13,692
Is it okay if we add one last thing?

392
00:28:14,276 --> 00:28:16,320
But we don't have any space left.

393
00:28:16,403 --> 00:28:17,863
Oh, that's not necessary.

394
00:28:18,405 --> 00:28:19,907
This paper will do.

395
00:28:21,283 --> 00:28:22,492
We can make a QR code

396
00:28:22,576 --> 00:28:26,288
and pair the random box
with a matching playlist.

397
00:28:26,872 --> 00:28:27,873
A playlist?

398
00:28:27,956 --> 00:28:31,418
Lighting and music are
what shape the mood of a space.

399
00:28:32,002 --> 00:28:35,130
If we link it to the user guide
and the review page

400
00:28:35,214 --> 00:28:37,090
it'll be easier to access everything.

401
00:28:38,217 --> 00:28:39,760
That'd be great
for collecting reviews.

402
00:28:40,010 --> 00:28:43,013
We could also add
a detailed survey and star ratings.

403
00:28:43,680 --> 00:28:47,017
Finally, I should put
my skills to use.

404
00:28:47,809 --> 00:28:51,438
- All right, Min-hyung. Go all out.
- Okay.

405
00:28:51,521 --> 00:28:53,023
- You've got this!
- You've got this!

406
00:28:53,774 --> 00:28:54,858
Show us!

407
00:29:15,170 --> 00:29:17,506
Why did you include the candle?

408
00:29:17,589 --> 00:29:19,258
You wouldn't give it up.

409
00:29:20,759 --> 00:29:23,971
I'll light the candle again
if you're not honest with me.

410
00:29:29,601 --> 00:29:31,728
The power went out
at the right moment

411
00:29:32,271 --> 00:29:34,064
and you showed up
at the right moment.

412
00:29:35,190 --> 00:29:37,401
I happened to be afraid of the dark

413
00:29:38,485 --> 00:29:40,529
and you brought up
your story about the rain.

414
00:29:40,612 --> 00:29:44,616
And at the center of it all
was just one little scented candle.

415
00:29:45,701 --> 00:29:47,411
I thought it wouldn't be so bad...

416
00:29:49,746 --> 00:29:51,999
if one candle from a random box

417
00:29:52,541 --> 00:29:54,668
could find its way
into someone's little coincidences

418
00:29:54,751 --> 00:29:56,545
be lit in the middle
of an ordinary moment

419
00:29:56,920 --> 00:30:00,382
and draw out feelings that help
two people open up to each other.

420
00:30:00,716 --> 00:30:02,384
"I liked our conversation
that night."

421
00:30:04,720 --> 00:30:07,681
You took the long way around
to say that.

422
00:30:11,977 --> 00:30:15,105
But why did you ask about <i>samgyetang?</i>

423
00:30:15,188 --> 00:30:16,189
What?

424
00:30:18,734 --> 00:30:20,402
Just because.

425
00:30:21,528 --> 00:30:23,572
It was just a random question.

426
00:30:26,908 --> 00:30:31,246
In fact, my grandpa
told me to invite someone.

427
00:30:33,206 --> 00:30:35,208
- Invite who?
- You, my blind date.

428
00:30:37,794 --> 00:30:39,254
- So?
- Well...

429
00:30:39,338 --> 00:30:40,589
I just don't think it's right.

430
00:30:41,089 --> 00:30:43,383
I keep delaying the date, but...

431
00:30:43,467 --> 00:30:45,677
Just tell him no
instead of dragging it out.

432
00:30:45,761 --> 00:30:47,304
You can't even push back that much?

433
00:30:48,013 --> 00:30:49,973
You've seen what my family's like.

434
00:30:50,057 --> 00:30:53,143
Grandpa's word is absolute.
I can't defy him.

435
00:30:53,518 --> 00:30:55,145
I can't push back.

436
00:31:00,275 --> 00:31:01,860
So I was wondering...

437
00:31:03,195 --> 00:31:06,406
Could you come in person

438
00:31:06,490 --> 00:31:08,325
and turn him down for me?

439
00:31:08,408 --> 00:31:09,409
No.

440
00:31:10,535 --> 00:31:11,787
Oh, I see.

441
00:31:12,662 --> 00:31:13,663
Absolutely.

442
00:31:14,164 --> 00:31:15,957
I'm sure you wouldn't want to.

443
00:31:21,296 --> 00:31:24,841
Actually, that was a selfish request.

444
00:31:24,925 --> 00:31:27,177
Forget I asked.

445
00:31:27,260 --> 00:31:28,512
I'll find a way...

446
00:31:30,180 --> 00:31:31,515
to deal with it on my own.

447
00:31:50,909 --> 00:31:52,035
I'm crazy.

448
00:31:52,119 --> 00:31:54,538
Why did I ask him to do that?

449
00:31:55,080 --> 00:31:58,583
I let my guard down fast
over one little candle.

450
00:32:01,294 --> 00:32:02,295
Ms. Gong.

451
00:32:03,463 --> 00:32:06,174
Mr. Yun, did you go somewhere?

452
00:32:07,384 --> 00:32:09,386
Ta-da. I did some fishing.

453
00:32:09,845 --> 00:32:12,097
It took me ages to find a stall
in this fall weather.

454
00:32:15,267 --> 00:32:17,102
You prefer fish-shaped pastries
to steamed buns.

455
00:32:17,185 --> 00:32:18,979
See how I left the bag open?

456
00:32:19,062 --> 00:32:20,230
That's so they wouldn't get soggy.

457
00:32:24,359 --> 00:32:26,403
Wait, are you a custard person,
not a red bean one?

458
00:32:26,653 --> 00:32:27,696
I can run back to grab those.

459
00:32:28,196 --> 00:32:29,614
No, it's okay.

460
00:32:30,532 --> 00:32:31,533
I like both.

461
00:32:34,661 --> 00:32:35,662
Have some.

462
00:32:36,621 --> 00:32:37,622
Thanks.

463
00:32:40,459 --> 00:32:41,460
Cheers.

464
00:32:45,005 --> 00:32:46,006
Oh, it's hot.

465
00:32:52,220 --> 00:32:54,931
There's nothing like this
when it's hot and fresh.

466
00:32:58,852 --> 00:33:00,770
Hey, Dal. You're still here.

467
00:33:01,980 --> 00:33:03,648
- Would you like one?
- I'm good.

468
00:33:03,732 --> 00:33:04,774
I should get dinner.

469
00:33:06,026 --> 00:33:07,110
Let's continue where we left off.

470
00:33:08,653 --> 00:33:10,113
- Sorry?
- Let's grab dinner.

471
00:33:20,582 --> 00:33:22,334
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

472
00:33:41,978 --> 00:33:43,355
I'll get straight to the point.

473
00:33:44,105 --> 00:33:46,358
Do you really need me
to turn him down?

474
00:33:47,692 --> 00:33:50,487
I told you I'd handle it myself.

475
00:33:50,570 --> 00:33:51,988
You don't need to worry about it.

476
00:33:52,072 --> 00:33:53,406
Let me put it differently.

477
00:33:54,574 --> 00:33:56,284
Have you ever, even once

478
00:33:56,535 --> 00:33:58,828
wanted to break one of the jars
in the yard?

479
00:34:00,330 --> 00:34:02,207
No, not really.

480
00:34:03,166 --> 00:34:05,043
Okay, I'll help you with that.

481
00:34:06,127 --> 00:34:09,589
First, think of something
the elders would disapprove of.

482
00:34:09,965 --> 00:34:12,801
Then we'll come up
with a specific plan.

483
00:34:19,224 --> 00:34:21,476
We've got so much work. I love it.

484
00:35:01,182 --> 00:35:03,101
<i>Anything other than picky eating?</i>

485
00:35:03,643 --> 00:35:04,644
Why?

486
00:35:04,728 --> 00:35:07,147
I used to get in so much trouble
for being a picky eater.

487
00:35:07,230 --> 00:35:10,400
Because I bet
your mother is a great cook.

488
00:35:15,238 --> 00:35:17,282
Let's be upfront about your job.

489
00:35:17,782 --> 00:35:18,825
Sounds good.

490
00:35:18,908 --> 00:35:20,577
But you can't mention me.

491
00:35:20,660 --> 00:35:23,038
Don't worry about that.
Anything else?

492
00:35:25,874 --> 00:35:29,336
He has one thing he values
above all else.

493
00:35:31,254 --> 00:35:33,757
"A man should be devoted
to his family

494
00:35:34,924 --> 00:35:35,967
and carry on the family line.

495
00:35:36,384 --> 00:35:38,803
A woman should obey her husband

496
00:35:38,887 --> 00:35:40,263
and bear children
to continue that line."

497
00:35:47,937 --> 00:35:49,648
That's quite intense, right?

498
00:35:50,190 --> 00:35:51,733
Should we think
of something less wild?

499
00:35:51,983 --> 00:35:54,069
No, it's fine. I can take it.

500
00:35:56,613 --> 00:35:58,448
So when's the date?

501
00:35:58,531 --> 00:35:59,574
This Saturday.

502
00:35:59,658 --> 00:36:01,284
- The time?
- At 12 p.m.

503
00:36:01,660 --> 00:36:04,120
Try coming 20 or 30 minutes late.

504
00:36:04,579 --> 00:36:07,749
My grandpa
absolutely hates tardiness.

505
00:36:07,999 --> 00:36:10,377
Got it. I'll take note.

506
00:36:28,895 --> 00:36:30,522
<i>The call cannot be connected...</i>

507
00:36:32,524 --> 00:36:33,942
What's going on?

508
00:36:34,025 --> 00:36:35,276
Why isn't she picking up?

509
00:36:36,653 --> 00:36:38,363
CALL LOG

510
00:36:38,446 --> 00:36:39,572
MY SI-EUN

511
00:36:39,656 --> 00:36:42,075
- It's pretty obvious.
- I agree.

512
00:36:43,993 --> 00:36:46,246
But where did Si-eun go?

513
00:36:46,329 --> 00:36:47,580
NAM-SU

514
00:36:47,664 --> 00:36:49,332
I think she went to the bathroom.

515
00:37:16,818 --> 00:37:17,819
He should be here soon, right?

516
00:37:20,488 --> 00:37:22,198
Oh, right. Baek-hee.

517
00:37:22,907 --> 00:37:24,826
Bring out the <i>seokbakji</i>
and green onion kimchi

518
00:37:24,909 --> 00:37:26,244
we made last week.

519
00:37:26,327 --> 00:37:27,829
- Yes, Mother.
- All right.

520
00:37:30,540 --> 00:37:32,709
Wasn't he supposed to be here
by noon?

521
00:37:33,084 --> 00:37:34,586
There's a lot of traffic these days.

522
00:37:35,044 --> 00:37:36,379
Don't be so impatient.

523
00:37:36,463 --> 00:37:37,464
Okay.

524
00:37:39,799 --> 00:37:41,384
Should we bring out
some ginseng liquor too?

525
00:37:41,801 --> 00:37:43,344
I wonder if he drinks.

526
00:37:48,433 --> 00:37:49,976
You're earlier than I expected.

527
00:37:50,059 --> 00:37:52,103
Well, it just worked out that way.

528
00:37:54,814 --> 00:37:56,983
- Shall we?
- Not yet.

529
00:37:57,275 --> 00:37:58,985
It's only 15 minutes late.

530
00:37:59,986 --> 00:38:01,821
Oh, I see.

531
00:38:05,533 --> 00:38:07,243
Good afternoon.

532
00:38:07,744 --> 00:38:09,204
Are you getting married?

533
00:38:10,038 --> 00:38:11,039
Oh, my.

534
00:38:11,414 --> 00:38:13,625
You used to be tiny,
and now you're getting married.

535
00:38:14,918 --> 00:38:16,961
- Bye.
- Did the second child

536
00:38:17,045 --> 00:38:18,880
in her family become
a civil servant yet?

537
00:38:18,963 --> 00:38:20,381
I don't think so.

538
00:38:30,600 --> 00:38:32,685
You look too neat.

539
00:38:33,394 --> 00:38:35,647
- Excuse me for a moment.
- Okay.

540
00:38:43,279 --> 00:38:44,739
This will do.

541
00:38:46,699 --> 00:38:49,160
- Oh, my word.
- Should I give her a call?

542
00:38:49,244 --> 00:38:51,037
Leave her be. She'll get here.

543
00:38:51,830 --> 00:38:52,831
Let's go in.

544
00:39:12,684 --> 00:39:13,893
We're here!

545
00:39:14,727 --> 00:39:16,062
Oh, they're here.

546
00:39:16,729 --> 00:39:17,939
Here they are.

547
00:39:35,415 --> 00:39:37,250
I hope it's to your taste.

548
00:39:38,167 --> 00:39:39,210
It's delicious, ma'am.

549
00:39:39,586 --> 00:39:41,671
I also loved the <i>cheonggukjang</i>
you made last time.

550
00:39:41,754 --> 00:39:43,590
You're such a great cook.

551
00:39:43,673 --> 00:39:45,925
Oh, aren't you sweet?

552
00:39:46,509 --> 00:39:48,052
I'll make it for you again sometime.

553
00:39:49,429 --> 00:39:52,348
- What do you like?
- I eat pretty much anything.

554
00:39:56,269 --> 00:39:57,312
(Don't forget.)

555
00:39:59,230 --> 00:40:02,400
As for chicken,
I prefer it boiled like <i>baeksuk.</i>

556
00:40:02,483 --> 00:40:05,153
And I only eat tender cuts of beef
like tenderloin.

557
00:40:06,487 --> 00:40:07,739
He's got refined tastes.

558
00:40:08,865 --> 00:40:11,326
Oh, I can't eat shellfish.

559
00:40:11,409 --> 00:40:12,660
I'm allergic.

560
00:40:14,203 --> 00:40:16,748
Shrimp too.
I'm allergic to that as well.

561
00:40:17,123 --> 00:40:18,374
Aside from that,
I'm not picky at all.

562
00:40:20,835 --> 00:40:23,046
Oh, right. I don't like eggplant.

563
00:40:23,755 --> 00:40:25,590
It's way too soft and mushy.

564
00:40:26,299 --> 00:40:29,802
I guess growing up privileged
made him a picky eater.

565
00:40:29,886 --> 00:40:32,388
Times are good now,
so people can afford to be picky.

566
00:40:32,472 --> 00:40:35,099
Back when we barely had enough to eat

567
00:40:35,183 --> 00:40:36,434
nobody could afford to be picky.

568
00:40:36,726 --> 00:40:39,270
We ate whatever
we could get our hands on

569
00:40:39,771 --> 00:40:40,897
even tree bark boiled in water.

570
00:40:41,898 --> 00:40:43,816
You're absolutely right

571
00:40:44,317 --> 00:40:46,569
but food that doesn't agree
with your body

572
00:40:46,653 --> 00:40:48,029
can do more harm than good.

573
00:40:51,699 --> 00:40:55,787
So what was it you said
your company does? Toys?

574
00:40:55,870 --> 00:40:57,914
Or was it exercise equipment?

575
00:41:01,167 --> 00:41:04,712
To be more precise,
we work in both areas.

576
00:41:05,088 --> 00:41:06,798
- Both areas?
- Yes.

577
00:41:08,549 --> 00:41:09,884
We make sex toys.

578
00:41:19,727 --> 00:41:21,145
What toys?

579
00:41:21,229 --> 00:41:23,773
Snack toys?

580
00:41:24,065 --> 00:41:25,942
No, ma'am. It's "sex."

581
00:41:28,069 --> 00:41:29,112
Sex toys.

582
00:41:29,278 --> 00:41:32,115
Put simply, you can think of them
as adult products.

583
00:41:32,407 --> 00:41:35,868
We import, make, and sell
a wide range of adult products.

584
00:41:36,160 --> 00:41:38,705
It suits my personality well,
so I enjoy what I do.

585
00:41:38,997 --> 00:41:40,206
You said it was a toy company.

586
00:41:40,665 --> 00:41:41,749
They are toys, sir.

587
00:41:42,083 --> 00:41:44,043
Kids play with toys

588
00:41:44,127 --> 00:41:47,171
for fun, comfort,
and emotional satisfaction.

589
00:41:47,672 --> 00:41:48,840
It's no different for adults.

590
00:41:49,424 --> 00:41:51,968
These are simply toys for adults.

591
00:41:52,218 --> 00:41:56,639
Well, times have changed a lot.

592
00:41:57,098 --> 00:42:01,894
Maybe it's just an area that
older folks like us don't quite get.

593
00:42:02,520 --> 00:42:04,063
You're very open-minded.

594
00:42:04,605 --> 00:42:06,524
Most people tend to have
prejudices about it.

595
00:42:06,607 --> 00:42:08,234
Oh, no prejudice at all.

596
00:42:08,317 --> 00:42:09,652
Well, okay.

597
00:42:18,661 --> 00:42:22,832
I hear your father runs
quite a large business.

598
00:42:23,166 --> 00:42:25,418
Do you plan to work with him someday?

599
00:42:26,419 --> 00:42:29,839
My father would like that,
but I have no intention of doing so.

600
00:42:30,256 --> 00:42:32,842
I'm genuinely passionate
about my business.

601
00:42:33,134 --> 00:42:36,471
Even so,
if you get married and have kids

602
00:42:36,554 --> 00:42:39,057
shouldn't you have
a respectable job as a parent?

603
00:42:40,099 --> 00:42:43,019
Thankfully, I won't have
to worry about that either.

604
00:42:43,478 --> 00:42:45,772
I'm azoospermic.

605
00:42:46,814 --> 00:42:50,193
So I probably won't ever have
children of my own.

606
00:42:52,695 --> 00:42:54,405
But what I'm really grateful for

607
00:42:54,489 --> 00:42:56,783
is that I have younger twin sisters
I absolutely adore.

608
00:42:57,033 --> 00:42:58,618
My father is getting older

609
00:42:58,701 --> 00:43:01,079
so I plan to raise them
as if they were my own.

610
00:43:06,501 --> 00:43:09,587
I'm perfectly functional
in every other way as a man

611
00:43:09,670 --> 00:43:10,963
so that's a relief.

612
00:43:18,805 --> 00:43:23,142
I mean, except for that,
he's practically perfect.

613
00:43:29,148 --> 00:43:30,316
I'll pour your drink, sir.

614
00:43:41,119 --> 00:43:44,122
I wish you nothing
but the best for the future.

615
00:43:45,331 --> 00:43:46,332
Thank you, sir.

616
00:43:54,215 --> 00:43:55,800
Thank you for today.

617
00:43:58,094 --> 00:44:01,556
I don't know if I should be
grateful for this, but I am.

618
00:44:01,639 --> 00:44:03,516
So thank you.

619
00:44:04,809 --> 00:44:05,810
Is that all?

620
00:44:06,853 --> 00:44:08,020
Honestly...

621
00:44:09,021 --> 00:44:10,523
I'm nervous about it.

622
00:44:11,440 --> 00:44:12,859
And a little scared.

623
00:44:12,942 --> 00:44:14,360
Not even a little cathartic?

624
00:44:18,865 --> 00:44:20,658
This was actually my first time.

625
00:44:21,450 --> 00:44:23,744
I've never thrown the elders off
like that before

626
00:44:23,828 --> 00:44:26,414
or messed up their plans.

627
00:44:28,749 --> 00:44:31,127
Your marriage, your partner's career

628
00:44:31,210 --> 00:44:33,337
their qualifications,
and having children...

629
00:44:33,754 --> 00:44:37,008
They planned it all
without your consent.

630
00:44:37,592 --> 00:44:39,218
You don't need to feel guilty.

631
00:44:42,889 --> 00:44:44,432
Is this what she meant?

632
00:44:46,100 --> 00:44:48,686
My aunt said she shouted for joy
outside the courthouse

633
00:44:49,061 --> 00:44:51,814
the day she filed for divorce.

634
00:44:52,398 --> 00:44:56,360
She said making such a huge,
life-changing decision for herself

635
00:44:56,444 --> 00:44:58,029
felt exhilarating.

636
00:44:58,613 --> 00:45:02,158
I'm starting to understand
how she felt.

637
00:45:02,867 --> 00:45:07,622
For the first time,
I felt this sense of freedom.

638
00:45:09,707 --> 00:45:10,833
That's good.

639
00:45:12,710 --> 00:45:15,922
You're honest and decisive, Ms. Gong.

640
00:45:16,839 --> 00:45:19,091
Live your own life
the way you'd market it.

641
00:45:19,926 --> 00:45:21,302
That's the way to go.

642
00:45:24,513 --> 00:45:26,724
Are you cheering me on right now?

643
00:45:26,807 --> 00:45:28,893
No, that was advice in disguise.

644
00:45:30,061 --> 00:45:32,438
But hear it however you like.

645
00:45:34,190 --> 00:45:37,068
I'm saying don't lose that bold,
slightly crazy side of you.

646
00:45:39,070 --> 00:45:41,447
No matter where you are.

647
00:45:43,991 --> 00:45:46,619
<i>This man is always testing me.</i>

648
00:45:46,702 --> 00:45:49,622
Anyway, that's all sorted out.

649
00:45:50,706 --> 00:45:53,042
We don't have to be tied together
as former blind dates anymore.

650
00:45:53,709 --> 00:45:56,337
And whatever connection
our families had is over too.

651
00:45:57,129 --> 00:45:59,882
We're completely out
of each other's personal lives now.

652
00:46:00,591 --> 00:46:04,428
So from here on out,
it's strictly business between us.

653
00:46:05,763 --> 00:46:09,934
<i>He barges in and shakes the handle</i>
<i>to my heart without warning.</i>

654
00:46:17,525 --> 00:46:19,944
You should go in.
I'll see you at the office.

655
00:46:32,456 --> 00:46:33,457
Mr. Dokgo.

656
00:46:52,560 --> 00:46:55,438
Would you like to go
on a date with me?

657
00:47:10,578 --> 00:47:14,498
<i>Our personal boundaries</i>
<i>have expanded.</i>

658
00:47:16,042 --> 00:47:20,046
MAKE ME TINGLE

659
00:47:35,895 --> 00:47:37,605
That's big trouble.

660
00:47:38,439 --> 00:47:39,899
Oh, my goodness.

661
00:47:56,832 --> 00:47:58,084
HORIZON
IT GETS CLEARER AS IT GOES FARTHER...

662
00:47:58,167 --> 00:47:59,710
RANDOM BOX

663
00:47:59,794 --> 00:48:01,337
IF I GET LOST, SO DOES THE BRAND!

664
00:48:05,341 --> 00:48:08,010
LOVE ISN'T ABOUT UNDERSTANDING
IT'S ABOUT ACCEPTANCE...

665
00:49:51,906 --> 00:49:53,908
Subtitles by Cherry Park
